Rem Capability: file
Rem ==================================================================
Rem seedrecio.shoddy — reckoner seed: recio.shoddy, over a resource
Rem held by NAME
Rem
Rem THE FIRST SEED TO OPEN SOMETHING. Every other seed in this directory
Rem takes values off the stack and puts values back; this one opens a
Rem file, keeps it open across lines, and shuts it when told. That was
Rem impossible until reckoner.shoddy grew a table of named resources —
Rem R3.5(b) kept handles off the stack because UNDO restores the stack
Rem and the number naming an open file would go with it. A NAME cannot
Rem be dropped, overwritten or undone away, so RECOPEN binds one and
Rem nothing ever pushes the handle.
Rem
Rem WHAT A SESSION HOLDS is therefore a string. "sales" RECCOUNT asks
Rem the file bound under "sales" how many records it has; CLOSE and
Rem BOUND are reckoner's own words and work here without this seed
Rem saying anything about them. There is no RECCLOSE, deliberately: one
Rem way to shut a resource is the whole reason the table is uniform.
Rem
Rem ---- THE LAYOUT PROBLEM, AND THE SHAPE OF THE ANSWER ---------------
Rem
Rem recio.shoddy asks for a record SIZE and a reader/writer pair over
Rem the caller's own Type:
Rem
Rem     Def rdstudent(f As Number) As Student
Rem         Student(GetStr(f, 12), GetNum(f))
Rem
Rem A host program writes those and compiles them in. A session cannot:
Rem there is no Type at a prompt and no way to write a Def there that
Rem the compiler has already seen. So this seed supplies ONE generic
Rem reader and ONE generic writer, and drives them from a SCHEMA the
Rem session types — a list of field specs:
Rem
Rem     { { "id" "number" } { "name" "str" 12 } { "paid" "bool" } }
Rem
Rem Three kinds, because three are what the runtime transfers: NUMBER is
Rem eight bytes, BOOL is one, and STR is a fixed zero-padded field whose
Rem width the spec carries. The record size is the sum, computed once at
Rem RECOPEN and kept with the binding, so no later word can disagree
Rem with the file about it.
Rem
Rem A RECORD IS A PLAIN LIST, in schema order — { 3 "GRACE" True } —
Rem and not a dict. A dict would be truer to the schema and worse to
Rem type: a session that has to build { ("id" 3) ("name" "GRACE") } to
Rem write one row will not write many. The names live in the schema,
Rem RECFIELDS answers them, and a session that wants a dict has
Rem seeddict's own words to make one.
Rem
Rem ---- WHY EVERY READ IS PRE-FLIGHTED --------------------------------
Rem
Rem GetNum, GetBool and GetStr all ABORT past the end of the file, and
Rem R3.5(a) does not allow a bridged word that can abort the session. So
Rem no read happens until the record number has been checked against
Rem RECCOUNT, which is BSize divided by the record size. A file whose
Rem length is not a whole number of records is refused at RECOPEN rather
Rem than at the first read, because that is a fact about the file and
Rem the earliest honest place to say so.
Rem
Rem THE FIELD LOOPS ARE EXPLICIT RECURSION rather than Map, because the
Rem transfers are SEQUENTIAL — each Get advances the position — and Map
Rem promises an answer per element, not an order to compute them in.
Rem Reading three fields is three effects that must happen in the order
Rem the schema lists them, so they are written as a fold that cannot be
Rem read any other way.
Rem ==================================================================

Include "recio.shoddy"
Include "cuttle.shoddy"
Include "reckoner.shoddy"
Include "seq.shoddy"

Rem ---- the schema -------------------------------------------------------

Rem One field: what it is called, which of the three kinds it is, and
Rem how many bytes it takes. Width is derived for NUMBER and BOOL and
Rem typed for STR, but it is stored for all three so the size
Rem arithmetic has one shape.
Type RecField
    FldName  As String
    FldKind  As String
    FldWidth As Number

Def RfName(x As RecField) As String
    FldName(x)

Def RfWidth(x As RecField) As Number
    FldWidth(x)

Def RcNumKind() As String
    "number"

Def RcStrKind() As String
    "str"

Def RcBoolKind() As String
    "bool"

Def RcKindWidth(kind As String) As Number
    If kind = RcNumKind() Then
        8
    Else
        If kind = RcBoolKind() Then
            1
        Else
            0

Rem ---- reading a schema off the stack -----------------------------------

Rem The whole schema, or the first thing wrong with it. Every refusal
Rem names the field by POSITION as well as by what was wrong, because a
Rem session that mistyped one spec in a list of six needs to be told
Rem which one.
Def RcSchemaOf(word As String, c As Cell) As Result
    Select Case RckListArg(word, c)
        Case Ok(specs)
            RcSchemaAt(word, specs, { }, 1)
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(w, at)
        Case Else
            Err(word & " did not answer", 0)

Def RcSchemaAt(word As String, specs As List Of Cell, acc As List Of RecField, k As Number) As Result
    If IsEmpty(specs) Then
        RcSchemaDone(word, acc)
    Else
        RcSchemaNext(word, specs, acc, k, RcFieldOf(word, First(specs), k))

Def RcSchemaDone(word As String, acc As List Of RecField) As Result
    If IsEmpty(acc) Then
        Err(word & ": A SCHEMA MUST HAVE AT LEAST ONE FIELD", 0)
    Else
        Ok(acc)

Def RcSchemaNext(word As String, specs As List Of Cell, acc As List Of RecField, k As Number, r As Result) As Result
    Select Case r
        Case Ok(f)
            RcSchemaAt(word, Rest(specs), Append(acc, f), k + 1)
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(w, at)
        Case Else
            Err(word & " did not answer", 0)

Def RcFieldWhy(word As String, k As Number) As String
    word & ": FIELD " & Str(k) & " MUST BE { name kind } OR { name \"" & RcStrKind() & "\" width }"

Def RcFieldOf(word As String, c As Cell, k As Number) As Result
    Select Case RckListArg(word, c)
        Case Ok(parts)
            RcFieldParts(word, parts, k)
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(RcFieldWhy(word, k), 0)
        Case Else
            Err(word & " did not answer", 0)

Def RcFieldParts(word As String, parts As List Of Cell, k As Number) As Result
    If Length(parts) < 2 Or Length(parts) > 3 Then
        Err(RcFieldWhy(word, k), 0)
    Else
        RcFieldNamed(word, parts, k)

Def RcFieldNamed(word As String, parts As List Of Cell, k As Number) As Result
    Select Case Pair(Nth(parts, 1), Nth(parts, 2))
        Case Pair(CutStr(nm), CutStr(kind))
            RcFieldKind(word, nm, Lower(kind), parts, k)
        Case Else
            Err(RcFieldWhy(word, k), 0)

Rem A STR field carries its own width and is the only kind that may; a
Rem NUMBER or BOOL given one is refused rather than ignored, because a
Rem width on those is a misunderstanding worth naming and not a
Rem harmless extra.
Def RcFieldKind(word As String, nm As String, kind As String, parts As List Of Cell, k As Number) As Result
    If kind = RcStrKind() Then
        RcFieldStr(word, nm, parts, k)
    Else
        RcFieldFixed(word, nm, kind, parts, k)

Def RcFieldFixed(word As String, nm As String, kind As String, parts As List Of Cell, k As Number) As Result
    If kind <> RcNumKind() And kind <> RcBoolKind() Then
        Err(word & ": FIELD " & Str(k) & " (" & nm & ") HAS KIND \"" & kind & "\" — IT MUST BE \"" & RcNumKind() & "\", \"" & RcStrKind() & "\" OR \"" & RcBoolKind() & "\"", 0)
    Else
        RcFieldPlain(word, nm, kind, parts, k)

Def RcFieldPlain(word As String, nm As String, kind As String, parts As List Of Cell, k As Number) As Result
    If Length(parts) <> 2 Then
        Err(word & ": FIELD " & Str(k) & " (" & nm & ") IS A " & Upper(kind) & " AND TAKES NO WIDTH — ONLY A \"" & RcStrKind() & "\" DOES", 0)
    Else
        Ok(RecField(nm, kind, RcKindWidth(kind)))

Def RcFieldStr(word As String, nm As String, parts As List Of Cell, k As Number) As Result
    If Length(parts) <> 3 Then
        Err(word & ": FIELD " & Str(k) & " (" & nm & ") IS A STRING AND NEEDS A WIDTH IN BYTES", 0)
    Else
        RcFieldWide(word, nm, Nth(parts, 3), k)

Def RcFieldWide(word As String, nm As String, wc As Cell, k As Number) As Result
    Select Case RckWholeArg(word, wc)
        Case Ok(w)
            RcFieldSized(word, nm, w, k)
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(word & ": FIELD " & Str(k) & " (" & nm & ") NEEDS A WHOLE WIDTH IN BYTES", 0)
        Case Else
            Err(word & " did not answer", 0)

Rem PutStr aborts on a string longer than its field, so a width of 0
Rem would make every write of a non-empty string fatal. Refused here,
Rem where the schema is being read, rather than at the first write.
Def RcFieldSized(word As String, nm As String, w As Number, k As Number) As Result
    If w < 1 Then
        Err(word & ": FIELD " & Str(k) & " (" & nm & ") NEEDS A WIDTH OF 1 BYTE OR MORE", 0)
    Else
        Ok(RecField(nm, RcStrKind(), w))

Rem ---- the schema, kept with the binding --------------------------------

Rem The schema goes into the resource's own data cell so that a word
Rem registered long before any open can find it from the name it is
Rem handed. It is stored as the SPEC LIST the session typed rather than
Rem as a List Of RecField, because a Cell is what the table carries and
Rem re-reading it is cheap next to the file access that follows.
Def RcKindName() As String
    "recio"

Def RcSize(fs As List Of RecField) As Number
    Fold(Map(fs, RfWidth), 0, +)

Def RcNames(fs As List Of RecField) As List Of String
    Map(fs, RfName)

Rem ---- finding the resource a word was named ----------------------------

Rem Every word below starts here: a name off the stack, the binding it
Rem refers to, and its schema read back. A name that is not bound is a
Rem refusal naming the name, which is the mistake a session actually
Rem makes — a typo, or a CLOSE it forgot it had done.
Def RcResult(word As String, st As RckState, c As Cell) As Result
    Select Case RckTextArg(word, c)
        Case Ok(nm)
            RcResAt(word, st, nm)
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(w, at)
        Case Else
            Err(word & " did not answer", 0)

Def RcResAt(word As String, st As RckState, nm As String) As Result
    If Not RckBoundTo(st, nm) Then
        Err(word & ": THERE IS NOTHING OPEN CALLED " & nm, 0)
    Else
        RcResKind(word, First(RckResOf(st, nm)), nm)

Rem A name bound by some OTHER machine is not this seed's to read. The
Rem kind is what tells them apart, and saying so beats reading a
Rem plotter's data cell as a record layout.
Def RcResKind(word As String, r As RckRes, nm As String) As Result
    If ResKindOf(r) <> RcKindName() Then
        Err(word & ": " & nm & " IS A " & Upper(ResKindOf(r)) & ", NOT A RECORD FILE", 0)
    Else
        Ok(r)

Rem ---- RECOPEN ----------------------------------------------------------

Rem RECOPEN is RckPureOver — the state as well as the arguments —
Rem because it has to answer TWO questions before it opens anything: is
Rem this name already taken, and is the file readable. Checking the name
Rem first is what stops the ordinary mistake (opening twice under one
Rem name) from costing a handle: reckoner's own backstop would shut the
Rem spare, but a word that never opens it is better than one that opens
Rem and closes it.
Def RcSeedOpen(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "RECOPEN", 3, RckPureOver(Fn(s, vs) => RcOpen(s, vs)), "( path schema name -- )", "Open a binary record file and keep it open under that name. The schema is a list of { name kind } specs, kind being \"number\" or \"bool\", or \"str\" with a width: { { \"id\" \"number\" } { \"who\" \"str\" 12 } }. CLOSE shuts it; BOUND lists what is open.")

Def RcOpen(st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case Pair(RckTextArg("RECOPEN", Nth(vs, 1)), RckTextArg("RECOPEN", Nth(vs, 3)))
        Case Pair(Ok(path), Ok(nm))
            RcOpenFree(st, path, Nth(vs, 2), nm)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("RECOPEN needs a path, a schema and a name")

Def RcOpenFree(st As RckState, path As String, sc As Cell, nm As String) As RckWork
    If RckBoundTo(st, nm) Then
        RckWorkBad("RECOPEN: THERE IS ALREADY SOMETHING OPEN CALLED " & nm)
    Else
        RcOpenSchema(path, sc, nm)

Def RcOpenSchema(path As String, sc As Cell, nm As String) As RckWork
    Select Case RcSchemaOf("RECOPEN", sc)
        Case Ok(fs)
            RcOpenMade(path, sc, nm, fs)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("RECOPEN did not answer")

Rem A record file is made if it is not there, because "open a new
Rem ledger" is an ordinary thing to want and an empty file is a valid
Rem one — RECCOUNT answers 0. TryWriteFile is the guarded create, and
Rem it only runs when the path is genuinely absent, so an existing file
Rem is never truncated by opening it.
Def RcOpenMade(path As String, sc As Cell, nm As String, fs As List Of RecField) As RckWork
    If Not FileExists(path) And Not TryWriteFile(path, "") Then
        RckWorkBad("RECOPEN: CANNOT MAKE '" & path & "'")
    Else
        RcOpenAt(path, sc, nm, fs)

Def RcOpenAt(path As String, sc As Cell, nm As String, fs As List Of RecField) As RckWork
    Select Case TryBOpen(path)
        Case Ok(f)
            RcOpenWhole(f, path, sc, nm, RcSize(fs))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad("RECOPEN: " & w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("RECOPEN did not answer")

Rem A file whose length is not a whole number of records is refused
Rem HERE, with the handle shut on the way out, rather than at the first
Rem read. It is a fact about the file and the schema together, so the
Rem moment they first meet is the earliest honest place to say it — and
Rem a session that opened the wrong schema on the right file finds out
Rem before it has written anything.
Def RcOpenWhole(f As Number, path As String, sc As Cell, nm As String, size As Number) As RckWork
    If BSize(f) - size * Floor(BSize(f) / size) <> 0 Then
        RcOpenRagged(f, path, size, BSize(f))
    Else
        RckOpened(nm, RcKindName(), f, sc, Fn() => RcShut(f))

Def RcOpenRagged(f As Number, path As String, size As Number, bytes As Number) As RckWork
    RcOpenSaid(RcShut(f), "RECOPEN: '" & path & "' IS " & Str(bytes) & " BYTES, WHICH IS NOT A WHOLE NUMBER OF " & Str(size) & "-BYTE RECORDS")

Rem The close happens for its effect and its answer is not the report;
Rem the report is the reason the file was refused.
Def RcOpenSaid(shut As Boolean, why As String) As RckWork
    If shut Then
        RckWorkBad(why)
    Else
        RckWorkBad(why)

Def RcShut(f As Number) As Boolean
    BClose(f)
    True

Rem ---- the words that read and write, all over a bound name -------------

Def RcSeedCount(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "RECCOUNT", 1, RckPureOver(Fn(s, vs) => RcCount(s, vs)), "( name -- n )", "How many records the file bound under that name holds.")

Def RcCount(st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RcResult("RECCOUNT", st, First(vs))
        Case Ok(r)
            RckVals({ CutNum(RcRecs(r)) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("RECCOUNT did not answer")

Def RcSeedFields(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "RECFIELDS", 1, RckPureOver(Fn(s, vs) => RcFields(s, vs)), "( name -- list )", "The field names of that file's schema, in the order a record lists them.")

Def RcFields(st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RcResult("RECFIELDS", st, First(vs))
        Case Ok(r)
            RcFieldsOf(r)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("RECFIELDS did not answer")

Def RcFieldsOf(r As RckRes) As RckWork
    Select Case RcSchemaOf("RECFIELDS", ResDataOf(r))
        Case Ok(fs)
            RckVals({ CutList(Map(RcNames(fs), CutStr)) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("RECFIELDS did not answer")

Rem The record count, from the handle and the schema the binding
Rem carries. Read rather than remembered, so a file the session has
Rem appended to answers its new length and not the one it opened with.
Def RcRecs(r As RckRes) As Number
    RcRecsAt(ResHandOf(r), RcSizeOf(r))

Def RcRecsAt(f As Number, size As Number) As Number
    Floor(BSize(f) / size)

Def RcSizeOf(r As RckRes) As Number
    RcSizeOr(RcSchemaOf("RECIO", ResDataOf(r)))

Rem The schema was validated at RECOPEN and stored as the session typed
Rem it, so this cannot fail — but it is read through a Result all the
Rem same, and a 1 rather than a 0 on the impossible branch, because a
Rem size of 0 would divide by zero and a wrong count is quieter than a
Rem dead mill.
Def RcSizeOr(r As Result) As Number
    Select Case r
        Case Ok(fs)
            RcSize(fs)
        Case Else
            1

Def RcSchemaFor(word As String, r As RckRes) As Result
    RcSchemaOf(word, ResDataOf(r))

Rem ---- RECGET, RECALL ---------------------------------------------------

Def RcSeedGet(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "RECGET", 2, RckPureOver(Fn(s, vs) => RcGet(s, vs)), "( name k -- rec )", "Record k of that file, as a list of values in schema order. Records number from 1; RECCOUNT is how many there are.")

Def RcGet(st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RcResult("RECGET", st, Nth(vs, 1))
        Case Ok(r)
            RcGetAt(r, Nth(vs, 2))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("RECGET did not answer")

Def RcGetAt(r As RckRes, kc As Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckWholeArg("RECGET", kc)
        Case Ok(k)
            RcGetWithin(r, k)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("RECGET did not answer")

Rem THE PRE-FLIGHT. Every Get aborts past the end of the file, so the
Rem record number is checked against the count before a single byte is
Rem read. RckWholeArg refuses negatives already, so 0 is the only low
Rem end left to catch.
Def RcGetWithin(r As RckRes, k As Number) As RckWork
    If k < 1 Or k > RcRecs(r) Then
        RckWorkBad("RECGET: THERE IS NO RECORD " & Str(k) & " — THE FILE HOLDS " & Str(RcRecs(r)))
    Else
        RcGetRead(r, k, RcSchemaFor("RECGET", r))

Def RcGetRead(r As RckRes, k As Number, sc As Result) As RckWork
    Select Case sc
        Case Ok(fs)
            RckVals({ RcReadRec(ResHandOf(r), k, RcSize(fs), fs) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("RECGET did not answer")

Def RcSeedAll(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "RECALL", 1, RckPureOver(Fn(s, vs) => RcAll(s, vs)), "( name -- list )", "Every record in that file, in file order, each one a list of values in schema order.")

Def RcAll(st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RcResult("RECALL", st, First(vs))
        Case Ok(r)
            RcAllOf(r, RcSchemaFor("RECALL", r))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("RECALL did not answer")

Def RcAllOf(r As RckRes, sc As Result) As RckWork
    Select Case sc
        Case Ok(fs)
            RckVals({ CutList(RcAllAt(ResHandOf(r), RcSize(fs), fs, RcRecs(r), 1, { })) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("RECALL did not answer")

Rem Explicit recursion rather than Map over Range, for the same reason
Rem the field loop below is: every record read moves the file position,
Rem so the order they are read in is the answer and not an incidental.
Def RcAllAt(f As Number, size As Number, fs As List Of RecField, n As Number, k As Number, acc As List Of Cell) As List Of Cell
    If k > n Then
        acc
    Else
        RcAllAt(f, size, fs, n, k + 1, Append(acc, RcReadRec(f, k, size, fs)))

Rem ---- RECPUT, RECAPPEND ------------------------------------------------

Def RcSeedPut(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "RECPUT", 3, RckPureOver(Fn(s, vs) => RcPut(s, vs)), "( name k rec -- )", "Write rec as record k, replacing what was there. rec is a list of values in schema order. k may be one past the end, which adds a record; anything beyond that is refused.")

Def RcPut(st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RcResult("RECPUT", st, Nth(vs, 1))
        Case Ok(r)
            RcPutAt(r, Nth(vs, 2), Nth(vs, 3))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("RECPUT did not answer")

Def RcPutAt(r As RckRes, kc As Cell, rec As Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckWholeArg("RECPUT", kc)
        Case Ok(k)
            RcPutWithin(r, k, rec)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("RECPUT did not answer")

Rem One past the end is allowed and anything further is not. Seek can
Rem go anywhere, so writing record 900 of a 3-record file would leave a
Rem hole of undefined bytes that reads back as garbage rather than as
Rem an error — a wrong answer, which is worse than a refusal.
Def RcPutWithin(r As RckRes, k As Number, rec As Cell) As RckWork
    If k < 1 Or k > RcRecs(r) + 1 Then
        RckWorkBad("RECPUT: RECORD " & Str(k) & " WOULD LEAVE A HOLE — THE FILE HOLDS " & Str(RcRecs(r)) & ", SO " & Str(RcRecs(r) + 1) & " IS THE FURTHEST YOU CAN WRITE")
    Else
        RcPutTyped(r, k, rec, RcSchemaFor("RECPUT", r))

Def RcPutTyped(r As RckRes, k As Number, rec As Cell, sc As Result) As RckWork
    Select Case sc
        Case Ok(fs)
            RcPutChecked("RECPUT", r, k, RckListArg("RECPUT", rec), fs)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("RECPUT did not answer")

Def RcPutChecked(word As String, r As RckRes, k As Number, vals As Result, fs As List Of RecField) As RckWork
    Select Case vals
        Case Ok(xs)
            RcPutMatched(word, r, k, xs, fs)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad(word & " did not answer")

Rem EVERY VALUE IS CHECKED AGAINST ITS FIELD BEFORE ANY OF THEM IS
Rem WRITTEN. A record half-written is a record corrupted, and PutStr
Rem aborts on an over-long string — so the whole row is validated first
Rem and the transfer only starts once nothing can refuse.
Def RcPutMatched(word As String, r As RckRes, k As Number, xs As List Of Cell, fs As List Of RecField) As RckWork
    If Length(xs) <> Length(fs) Then
        RckWorkBad(word & ": THE RECORD HAS " & Str(Length(xs)) & " VALUES AND THE SCHEMA HAS " & Str(Length(fs)) & " FIELDS")
    Else
        RcPutSound(word, r, k, xs, fs, RcWhyRow(word, xs, fs, 1))

Def RcPutSound(word As String, r As RckRes, k As Number, xs As List Of Cell, fs As List Of RecField, why As String) As RckWork
    If why <> "" Then
        RckWorkBad(why)
    Else
        RcPutWrote(word, r, k, xs, fs)

Def RcPutWrote(word As String, r As RckRes, k As Number, xs As List Of Cell, fs As List Of RecField) As RckWork
    RcWroteRec(ResHandOf(r), k, RcSize(fs), fs, xs)
    RckVals({ })

Def RcSeedAppend(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "RECAPPEND", 2, RckPureOver(Fn(s, vs) => RcAppend(s, vs)), "( name rec -- k )", "Add rec to the end of that file and push the record number it became.")

Def RcAppend(st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RcResult("RECAPPEND", st, Nth(vs, 1))
        Case Ok(r)
            RcAppendAt(r, Nth(vs, 2))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("RECAPPEND did not answer")

Def RcAppendAt(r As RckRes, rec As Cell) As RckWork
    RcAppendTyped(r, RcRecs(r) + 1, rec, RcSchemaFor("RECAPPEND", r))

Def RcAppendTyped(r As RckRes, k As Number, rec As Cell, sc As Result) As RckWork
    Select Case sc
        Case Ok(fs)
            RcAppendChecked(r, k, RckListArg("RECAPPEND", rec), fs)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("RECAPPEND did not answer")

Def RcAppendChecked(r As RckRes, k As Number, vals As Result, fs As List Of RecField) As RckWork
    Select Case vals
        Case Ok(xs)
            RcAppendMatched(r, k, xs, fs)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("RECAPPEND did not answer")

Def RcAppendMatched(r As RckRes, k As Number, xs As List Of Cell, fs As List Of RecField) As RckWork
    If Length(xs) <> Length(fs) Then
        RckWorkBad("RECAPPEND: THE RECORD HAS " & Str(Length(xs)) & " VALUES AND THE SCHEMA HAS " & Str(Length(fs)) & " FIELDS")
    Else
        RcAppendSound(r, k, xs, fs, RcWhyRow("RECAPPEND", xs, fs, 1))

Def RcAppendSound(r As RckRes, k As Number, xs As List Of Cell, fs As List Of RecField, why As String) As RckWork
    If why <> "" Then
        RckWorkBad(why)
    Else
        RcAppendWrote(r, k, xs, fs)

Def RcAppendWrote(r As RckRes, k As Number, xs As List Of Cell, fs As List Of RecField) As RckWork
    RcWroteRec(ResHandOf(r), k, RcSize(fs), fs, xs)
    RckVals({ CutNum(k) })

Rem ---- checking a row against the schema --------------------------------

Rem "" for nothing wrong, so a caller reads one string rather than
Rem unwrapping a Result at four call sites. The position is carried so
Rem the message can name WHICH field, which is the whole difference
Rem between a usable refusal and "that record is wrong".
Def RcWhyRow(word As String, xs As List Of Cell, fs As List Of RecField, k As Number) As String
    If IsEmpty(fs) Then
        ""
    Else
        RcWhyNext(word, xs, fs, k, RcWhyOne(word, First(xs), First(fs), k))

Def RcWhyNext(word As String, xs As List Of Cell, fs As List Of RecField, k As Number, why As String) As String
    If why <> "" Then
        why
    Else
        RcWhyRow(word, Rest(xs), Rest(fs), k + 1)

Def RcWhyOne(word As String, c As Cell, x As RecField, k As Number) As String
    If FldKind(x) = RcNumKind() Then
        RcWhyNum(word, c, x, k)
    Else
        If FldKind(x) = RcBoolKind() Then
            RcWhyBool(word, c, x, k)
        Else
            RcWhyStr(word, c, x, k)

Def RcWhyAt(word As String, x As RecField, k As Number, wanted As String) As String
    word & ": FIELD " & Str(k) & " (" & FldName(x) & ") WANTS " & wanted

Def RcWhyNum(word As String, c As Cell, x As RecField, k As Number) As String
    Select Case c
        Case CutNum(v)
            ""
        Case Else
            RcWhyAt(word, x, k, "A NUMBER")

Def RcWhyBool(word As String, c As Cell, x As RecField, k As Number) As String
    Select Case c
        Case CutBool(v)
            ""
        Case Else
            RcWhyAt(word, x, k, "TRUE OR FALSE")

Def RcWhyStr(word As String, c As Cell, x As RecField, k As Number) As String
    Select Case c
        Case CutStr(v)
            RcWhyFits(word, v, x, k)
        Case Else
            RcWhyAt(word, x, k, "A STRING")

Rem PutStr ABORTS on a string longer than its field rather than
Rem truncating, so this is the guard that keeps a long name from ending
Rem the session. Measured in BYTES, because that is what the field
Rem holds and what PutStr counts.
Def RcWhyFits(word As String, v As String, x As RecField, k As Number) As String
    If Len(v) > FldWidth(x) Then
        word & ": FIELD " & Str(k) & " (" & FldName(x) & ") HOLDS " & Str(FldWidth(x)) & " BYTES AND THAT STRING IS " & Str(Len(v))
    Else
        ""

Rem ---- the transfers ----------------------------------------------------

Rem Reading and writing one record, field by field, in schema order.
Rem RecSeek puts the position at the start of record k and every Get and
Rem Put advances it, so these two walk the row exactly as recio's own
Rem examples do — the difference is only that the field list is data
Rem here and code there.

Def RcReadRec(f As Number, k As Number, size As Number, fs As List Of RecField) As Cell
    RecSeek(f, k, size)
    CutList(RcReadFields(f, fs, { }))

Def RcReadFields(f As Number, fs As List Of RecField, acc As List Of Cell) As List Of Cell
    If IsEmpty(fs) Then
        acc
    Else
        RcReadOn(f, fs, acc, RcReadOne(f, First(fs)))

Def RcReadOn(f As Number, fs As List Of RecField, acc As List Of Cell, c As Cell) As List Of Cell
    RcReadFields(f, Rest(fs), Append(acc, c))

Def RcReadOne(f As Number, x As RecField) As Cell
    If FldKind(x) = RcNumKind() Then
        CutNum(GetNum(f))
    Else
        If FldKind(x) = RcBoolKind() Then
            CutBool(GetBool(f))
        Else
            CutStr(GetStr(f, FldWidth(x)))

Def RcWroteRec(f As Number, k As Number, size As Number, fs As List Of RecField, xs As List Of Cell)
    RecSeek(f, k, size)
    RcWriteFields(f, fs, xs)

Def RcWriteFields(f As Number, fs As List Of RecField, xs As List Of Cell)
    If Not IsEmpty(fs) Then
        RcWriteOn(f, fs, xs)

Def RcWriteOn(f As Number, fs As List Of RecField, xs As List Of Cell)
    RcWriteOne(f, First(fs), First(xs))
    RcWriteFields(f, Rest(fs), Rest(xs))

Rem The row was checked against the schema before anything was written,
Rem so the Else here is unreachable rather than lenient — it writes the
Rem field's worth of nothing so the record stays its stated size, which
Rem is the only answer that keeps the file readable.
Def RcWriteOne(f As Number, x As RecField, c As Cell)
    Select Case c
        Case CutNum(v)
            PutNum(f, v)
        Case CutBool(v)
            PutBool(f, v)
        Case CutStr(v)
            PutStr(f, v, FldWidth(x))
        Case Else
            PutStr(f, "", FldWidth(x))

Rem ---- the seed ---------------------------------------------------------

Def RckSeedRecio(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let s1 = RcSeedOpen(RckSeeding(st, "seed-recio"))
    Let s2 = RcSeedCount(s1)
    Let s3 = RcSeedFields(s2)
    Let s4 = RcSeedGet(s3)
    Let s5 = RcSeedAll(s4)
    Let s6 = RcSeedPut(s5)
    RcSeedAppend(s6)
